# Random modules whose polymorphic predicates and functions call each
# other and library predicates at types that bind the callees' type
# variables to the callers' own, to types without variables and to types
# built from both, and test and compare values of type variables
# (generate-polymorphic-programs.py). merkc must give each procedure the
# hidden type_info arguments that mmc does, and each call the type_infos
# for the same types.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-polymorphic-programs.py --seed 12 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-polymorphism %t/*.m
